{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-classical-limit-functor","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:classical-limit-functor","kind":"definition","title":"The classical limit functor $q \\to 1$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-parameter-planck","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-adelic-substrate"],"tags":["classical-limit","functor","q-to-1","deformation","symmetric-monoidal","adelic-assembly","realization-tower"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor","text":"classical-limit-functor.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-functor.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:classical-limit-functor\"></a><p>Define the <strong>classical limit</strong> as a <a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-monoidal-functor\">monoidal functor</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L} : \\mathbf{C}_q \\longrightarrow \\mathbf{C}_1</code> from the <a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-braided-monoidal-category\">braided monoidal category</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}_q</code> (at deformation parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>) to the <a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-symmetric-monoidal-category\">symmetric monoidal category</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}_1</code> (at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code>). The functor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}</code> acts on the substrate algebra by:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Quantum gap collapse</strong>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hbar_q = 1 - q^{-1} \\to 0</code>, so that the non-commutativity vanishes.</li>\n<li><strong>Differential smoothing</strong>: The Jackson <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-derivative <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q f(z)</code> converges to the ordinary derivative <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\frac{df}{dz}</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Braiding trivialization</strong>: The braiding <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_{X,Y}</code> specializes to the symmetric swap <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau_{X,Y}</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The functor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}</code> is exact but not full: quantum information is lost in the limit.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-functor.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"20.4.1"}
